      "widgets_values": [
        "TRANSPARENT DECAL + STENCIL\n\nEdit the green prompt to describe one isolated subject. Keep a plain white background and empty margin. Run to save an RGBA PNG plus a grayscale stencil.\n\nBiRefNet removes the background locally. White in the stencil means visible; black means hidden. Soft gray edges preserve antialiasing.\n\nStart at 512x512 for this SD1.5 model; try 768x768 for more detail. These are cutout decals, leaves, ornaments or texture stamps. For full surface tiles use the original workflow.\n\nIn Blender connect Image Color to Base Color and Alpha to shader Alpha. Enable transparency in your material if required by your 3D app."
      ]
